{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:7872284 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:7872284 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"7872284","source":"MED","pmid":"7872284","title":"Prevention of beta-lactam-associated diarrhea by Saccharomyces boulardii compared with placebo.","authorString":"McFarland LV, Surawicz CM, Greenberg RN, Elmer GW, Moyer KA, Melcher SA, Bowen KE, Cox JL.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"McFarland LV","lastName":"McFarland","firstName":"L V","initials":"LV","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Medicinal Chemistry, University of Washington, Seattle."}]}},{"fullName":"Surawicz CM","lastName":"Surawicz","firstName":"C M","initials":"CM"},{"fullName":"Greenberg RN","lastName":"Greenberg","firstName":"R N","initials":"RN"},{"fullName":"Elmer GW","lastName":"Elmer","firstName":"G W","initials":"GW"},{"fullName":"Moyer KA","lastName":"Moyer","firstName":"K A","initials":"KA"},{"fullName":"Melcher SA","lastName":"Melcher","firstName":"S A","initials":"SA"},{"fullName":"Bowen KE","lastName":"Bowen","firstName":"K E","initials":"KE"},{"fullName":"Cox JL","lastName":"Cox","firstName":"J L","initials":"JL"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","wikipedia"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"3","volume":"90","journalIssueId":848873,"dateOfPublication":"1995 Mar","monthOfPublication":3,"yearOfPublication":1995,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Am J Gastroenterol","title":"The American journal of gastroenterology","essn":"1572-0241","issn":"0002-9270","isoabbreviation":"Am J Gastroenterol","nlmid":"0421030"},"printPublicationDate":"1995-03-01"},"pubYear":"1995","pageInfo":"439-448","abstractText":"<h4>Objectives</h4>To determine the safety and efficacy of a new preventive agent for antibiotic-associated diarrhea (AAD) in patients receiving at least one beta-lactam antibiotic.<h4>Methods</h4>A double-blinded, placebo-controlled, parallel group study was performed in a high-risk group of hospitalized patients receiving a new prescription for a beta-lactam antibiotic and having no acute diarrhea on enrollment. Lyophilized Saccharomyces boulardii or placebo (1 g/day) was given within 72 h of the start of the antibiotic(s) and continued until 3 days after the antibiotic was discontinued, after which the patients were followed for 7 wk.<h4>Results</h4>Of the 193 eligible patients, significantly fewer, 7/97 (7.2%), patients receiving S. boulardii developed AAD compared with 14/96 (14.6%) on placebo (p = 0.02). The efficacy of S. boulardii for the prevention of AAD was 51%. Using a multivariate model to adjust for two independent risk factors for AAD (age and days of cephalosporin use), the adjusted relative risk was significantly protective for S. boulardii (RR = 0.29, 95% CI = 0.08, 0.98).<h4>Conclusion</h4>The prophylactic use of S. boulardii given with a beta-lactam antibiotic resulted in a significant reduction of AAD with no serious adverse reactions.","affiliation":"Department of Medicinal Chemistry, University of Washington, Seattle.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Comparative Study","Clinical Trial","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Multicenter Study","Randomized Controlled Trial","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Saccharomyces"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Diarrhea","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"CI","qualifierName":"chemically induced"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"EP","qualifierName":"epidemiology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"PC","qualifierName":"prevention & control"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"beta-Lactams"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Anti-Bacterial Agents","meshQualifierList":{"mes